Z||000000||soup||12-13-2001||01:20 AM||||My speedo light does not work, hasn't since  bought the car last month. I cant find a bulb in the back that lights up the speedo, do i actually need to take out the speedo to access the light? Do i need to get a new speedo? <P>thanks in advance<BR>Soup||||reg||5
Z||000001||GTDude||12-15-2001||08:43 PM||||You should be able to take the back off of the instrument panel and you should be able to see the back of the panel.  It's a white plastic case with a printed circuit.  There should be about 9 bulbs if I remember correctly.  I believe that 3 actually illuminate the speedometer.  It's possible that the printed circuit is burned out so check it with a test light and see if you have current to the bulbs. If not then the printed circuit is bad.  Let me know when you get this far, or if you need any more help.<P>Phil<P>------------------<BR>GTDude's 86GT||||reg||3
Z||000002||soup||12-16-2001||09:10 PM||||hey, <BR>I had tested all the bulbs before, but that wassnt the problem, they are all lit up. I havent had a lot of time to spend on it, but when looking at it, the tach (which lights up) has an orange piece with a hole cut for the light to shine through. It doesnt look as though my speedo has any holes cut for the light to shine through on this orange peice. When I get the time I will take the whole dash apart and see if I can take out the speedo to give it a better inspection. Thanks for the tips though.||||reg||1
